From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthony Fu <github@antfu.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:50:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): clone a project from another connected host

Moving a project to another machine meant finding its remote URL on the
first host and pasting it into "Clone from GitHub" on the second. With
more than one host connected, Add project now offers "Clone from other
host": it lists the git projects on the other connected hosts (minus the
ones this host already has), and picking one continues with the usual
clone steps, destination and name, using the project's remote. The remote
comes from one of the project's workspaces, or else from its `remote:`
project key.

New workspace uses it too. A host without the selected project looked like
any other host there, and picking it silently lost the project. Its row in
the host picker now says "(project not exists)", and an online one has a
Setup button, which opens Add project on that host at "Clone from other
host", already searching for the project, so it can be cloned there in a
few steps.

Fork-Change: F-11
